WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Steep slopes produce angular rock fragments. Flowing water carries

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.540
sediment into channels, while floods spread finer material across

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.840
a floodplain. Watch the grains move; the setting is

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.260
defined by its transport and deposition, not just its

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.680
location. When the river enters standing water, it slows.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.480
Coarser sediment accumulates near the mouth, building a delta.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.880
Finer particles can remain suspended and travel farther. A

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.140
delta and a floodplain are different parts of the

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.820
river system. Waves work the beach. A barrier shelters

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.500
a lagoon. Offshore, fine material settles, and sediment-laden turbidity

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.520
currents can move downslope. Compare grain size, structures, and

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.360
biological remains before choosing an ancient environment.
